      "“Mom…” he began slowly. “Mom, you’re already married. And you’re a woman.”",
      "Why did I say that? he thought, internally slamming his head against an imaginary wall. Why does my mouth insist on driving without a licence?",
      "Wardah rose from the cushions, circled the coffee table with predatory calm, and delivered a solid, affectionate thud to his shoulder blade. “Dumbo. It’s for you.”",
      "“For me?” His voice cracked right down the middle, leaping an entire octave. “Marriage? Now? Mom, how old am I? I’m thirteen. It’s child labour. It’s illegal.”",
      "“You are twenty-one.”",
      "“I am emotionally thirteen!”",
      "“That, Alhamdulillah, I believe.”",
      "In the quiet corner of his chest, a calmer voice—annoyingly rational and sounding suspiciously like his mother—whispered: Come on. It’s time.",
      "He felt a tremor in his fingertips, born from an overwhelming cocktail of shock, sudden excitement, and the stark reality that nobody had warned him it was Marriage Day when he had only eaten one slice of toast. “F-for m-me? Really?”",
      "“Really,” Wardah said, her eyes softening with warmth. “It’s time for some maturity and responsibility. Go wash your face, fix your hair, and come sit down to choose.”",
      "“Yes, ma’am,” Ma’un blurted out, stiffening into an accidental military posture. Nobody in the history of this household had ever uttered the words 'yes, ma’am.'",
      "Wardah chuckled fondly. “Oh, look at that. Is the big boy shy?”",
      "He fled down the hallway.",
      "Ten minutes later, with cold water splashed across his cheeks and his collar once again rearranged into a fresh variety of crooked, Ma’un sat on the sofa. Around him, his family assembled like a tribunal.",
      "Dania took the armchair, curled up sideways with her phone resting against her knee, radiating the calm authority of a senior detective reviewing a case file. Hana slid in last, folding her legs beneath her on the carpet with her white earphones draped loosely around her neck like a scarf, skimming through the resumes as if ordering takeout.",
      "“Big bro,” Dania said, holding up a cream-coloured document, “this one looks ideal for you. Very 'I alphabetise my spice rack and colour-code my socks.'”",
      "Hana, determined not to be outdone, flicked another profile across the glass table. “Look at this one—super polite, top marks, and noticeably shorter than you. Wait. Bro. What are your actual preferences in girls?”",
      "Ma’un parted his lips. My preferences are…",
      "My preferences are…",
      "He drew a complete blank. He searched the filing cabinets of his mind; the drawers were entirely bare. Years of devoutly lowering his gaze on campus and avoiding casual small talk had worked so remarkably well that he had literally never compiled any market research.",
      "“I don’t have any preferences,” he confessed at last, his cheeks pinking. “I just… I kept being religious and lowered my gaze, and I never really thought about that kind of stuff.”",
      "“That is so painfully you,” Hana remarked with genuine, wide-eyed respect. “Heart of gold, zero game. But maybe don’t lead with that when we meet them.”",
      "“Alternative proposal,” Dania chimed in from the armchair, tapping her screen. “Darts. We tape the pictures to the wall, big bro throws blindfolded, and whoever he hits, we call.”",
      "“We are not selecting your brother’s life partner with pub games,” Wardah said firmly.",
      "“I already brought the board,” Hana announced, having materialized from the corner holding a bristled dartboard with a faded anime poster taped across its center. “Sorry, Sensei,” she whispered solemnly to the printed villain.",
      "Wardah confiscated the dartboard with the effortless authority of a mother who had seized contrabands from childhood bedrooms for twenty years. “We choose like respectable, civilized believers. With phone calls, polite inquiries, tea, and far too many intrusive questions.” She drew a single folder from beneath the stack and set it squarely in front of Ma’un. “And I’ve already taken the liberty. This family called me twice before I’d even turned off the stove this morning.”",
      "“Suspiciously efficient,” Dania murmured, narrowing her eyes.",
      "“Desperation is a major red flag,” Hana declared.",
      "“Eager,” Wardah corrected with a pointed look, “is simply a family that knows what it wants. We shall see. Just a little while, Ma’un. A few days of calls, and then we go visit.”",
      "Ma’un stared at the closed folder. He didn’t open it. Not yet. He had a personal principle: ask the foundational questions first.",
      "“What is she like?” he asked softly.",
      "“I don’t know,” Wardah replied honestly. “That is what the visit is for.”",
      "“What’s her name?”",
      "“Naba.”",
      "He repeated it once, under his breath, barely parting his lips. *Naba.*",
      "It sat in his mouth like a word he had known in a dream—familiar, gentle, waiting to be uncovered.",
      "Ma’un nodded slowly, looking out the sunlit window at the bustling street below. He had never met her in his life.",
      "(He had, actually. For eleven breathless seconds, that very morning, in the middle of a crowded pavement outside the pharmacy, apologising for existing.",
      "The narrator promised itself it would not reveal more, and is already deeply regretting it.)"
